VERDICT: REJECTED
The diff is not ready to mark complete because the new theme-selection UX is implemented in the wrong screen path and is not reliably reachable in the active app flow.

Critical findings:
- The 3-way Light/Auto/Dark toggle was added to `app/(tabs)/explore.tsx`, but the root navigation still targets `/explore` from `app/_layout.tsx` and the project still has a separate `app/explore.tsx`. In this routing setup, the user-facing Settings route can remain the root `app/explore.tsx` (which was not upgraded with the toggle), so the core feature (“user can override theme in Settings”) is not assured in the primary path.
- The theme context/provider and hook delegation are implemented and typecheck successfully, but without the Settings control being correctly wired to the active route, the feature is functionally incomplete from a user perspective.
- The commit range also includes very large unrelated deletions/changes under `.local/**` and `.replit`; these are out of scope for the stated feature and create avoidable risk/noise for task acceptance.

Security:
- None observed.

Next actions:
1) Put the theme toggle in the actual user-facing Settings route (or make routing unambiguously use the `(tabs)` Settings screen) and align all `router.push('/explore')` targets accordingly.
2) Verify behavior end-to-end: switch theme, restart app (web + native), confirm persisted preference and correct System fallback.
3) Revert/split unrelated `.local/**` and `.replit` churn from this task’s deliverable so review focuses on intended product changes only.

